{
  "_about": "AO1990 Base IV (consonantal sequences). Chiefly the c/p sequences -cc-, -cç-, -ct-, -pc-, -pç-, -pt-, plus the parallel b/g/m/t oscillations (subtil/sutil, súbdito/súdito, amígdala/amídala). Three classes: kept everywhere (pronounced in all norms), dropped everywhere (mute in all norms), and dual (pronounced in one norm, mute in another -> both spellings are official, one per norm). This classification is irreducibly lexical: it cannot be derived by regex. NB the dual direction is NOT always 'PT drops': for 'corrupto/corruto' the European norm pronounces (and keeps) the p while Brazil may drop it.",
